  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-mcp-market",
      "text": "[中文](README.zh.md) | English\n\nAn **MCP server marketplace** inside DeepSeek Harness: browse a curated catalog and install MCP servers into the running profile with one click — **live, no restart** (powered by the official `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` and the loader service).\n\nOpen **Settings → MCP Market**, search, click, done. The model immediately sees `mcp__<serverName>__<tool>` tools."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Browse / search / filter a bundled catalog (15 servers, every one verified usable), zh/en descriptions\n- npm existence verification: every stdio entry is checked against registry.npmjs.org at load time; packages removed from the registry are greyed out and blocked from install (guards against dead entries and typosquat canaries)\n- One-click install for `stdio` (local process) and `streamable-http` (remote URL); fill in command / args / env / url / headers before installing\n- Hot activation via `ctx.loader.create()` — no restart; config persists across restarts\n- Installed list with enable/disable, config edit (HMR reconnect), and uninstall\n- Manual \"add a server\" form for anything not in the catalog\n- Offline fallback: remote registry JSON with an in-memory cache and a bundled snapshot\n- Clean persistence: installs only touch a `# --- dsh-mcp-market managed ---` block in the profile's `cordis.patch.yml`; your own edits are preserved verbatim"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "from npm (for everyone)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-mcp-market"
    },
    {
      "section": "from a local checkout (dev only — replace the path with yours)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add \"D:\\path\\to\\dsh-mcp-market\""
    },
    {
      "section": "update",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web update dsh-mcp-market"
    },
    {
      "section": "remove",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-mcp-market\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web`, then open **Settings → MCP Market**."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run build        # tsc host → lib/, esbuild client → client/client.js\nnpm run typecheck\n```\n\nAfter changes: `npm run build`, restart `dsh web` (host changes; client changes can use a dev watcher)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Registry source",
      "text": "Live catalog: fetched from the GitHub Pages URL `https://LKMeng2001.github.io/dsh-mcp-market/servers.json` (canonical source is `docs/servers.json` in this repo — edit and push to update globally, no release needed), falling back to the bundled `data/registry-snapshot.json` (generated from `docs/servers.json` by `npm run sync:catalog`). A CI workflow checks every npm package in the catalog daily. Override per profile via the plugin config (`registryUrl`). Entry schema and the HTTP route/loader design are documented in [README.zh.md](README.zh.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security",
      "text": "- Every mutating route is a **same-origin POST** with Origin checks\n- MCP servers are third-party code/services: stdio servers spawn a local child process — install only sources you trust\n- Config (incl. env) is stored in plaintext in the profile's `cordis.patch.yml`; keep secrets out or encrypt before writing"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
